  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Finite bit-circuit construction and exact frozen-class minimum; no new kappa.** On PR1062's frozen 11,500-ADD R439 word, the restored noncommuting chain `a ^= b; b ^= c` reduces the complete scalar invoice to **11,489**. Its individual complete gains are **0 and -1**; together it removes fifteen middle ADDs and pays all four new preparation/restoration gates. The correct middle substitution and reverse-order undo are explicit.\n\nTwo code-disjoint complete score censuses agree on **77,431,469** eligible triples, **2265** improvements and exactly two eleven-ADD maximizers. All eligible records share digest `142ad23bdd285011e5090ed40b57af69386e7a8c1f259548e83eba66f3f339f3`. The first 32 seed-ordered positive nominees receive complete invoices; all pass. An admitted maximizer proves the exact minimum in this stated class, not global circuit optimality or a best-known count. A separate written support inequality bounds the interaction; finite replay is not formal verification of multiplication.\n\nThe winning full-word peaks are **F=25885, B=5977064**: sufficient **96 local /182 nine-stage bits**, below both original strict 104/192 caps. The 2,911 MOVEs, nine COPYs and nine ERASEs, 439 dirty helper roles and rank mass 5,129 remain unchanged. No paid-moment or selected-supplier improvement follows. H2 and literal K_equals_D remain false as in the parent; native/whole-hosted admission and full supplier/outer invoices are unrun.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nFresh OS **seed 17**, bit supplier; base **ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6**. Scope **changed** from bit-helper-contract because PR1194/1311 already cover semantic-D substitution. This scalar side result tests a different mechanism: two helper/right shears with nonpositive frozen unilateral gains, on three distinct non-retained parent components. All other fields are fixed. [Local claim/result](https://github.com/ToikY/integer-mult-bounds/blob/8d17ec366d4e4e50d8f28fdb3f23cf9213417b7a/research/r439-neutral-helper-chain-seed17/CLAIM.json) records three candidates, closed domain and stopping rule. No pinned sprint issue was identified; the user-permitted local fallback is used.\n\nExact heads: PR1062 **cd016e5dcd5ba28dafa3f3b4eeef003a38e6a11b**; PR965 **6292e3774abd82f2d5202190b498f35cc1628c39**; PR1449 **52a487a0c85e83d875f30a74f795588399bac093**; PR1400 **2515ad2fa93eca3d64523bc55fd70eca08c9aa4b**. [PR1449](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1449) concerns one target plus one helper on PR967; [PR1400](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1400) uses individually positive descent on PR1047; PR965's GL3 region and PR1206's R420 chains differ. Their mechanisms are credited and their savings are not combined.\n\nThe final refresh read newest 20 open PR bodies through PR1538, all 15 helper/noncommuting keyword matches, the current Discussion first page and pinned start thread. PR1520's J3 precision frontier and PR1535's B509 inverse-frame audit concern different obligations. An immediate recheck reached PR1541\u2019s different coordinate-swap theorem. This is bounded overlap evidence; not all PRs/comments were freshly paginated. Upstream reached **55a02580ce1b283026e9d3b3510b218f8c93a4de**; guidance and all ten consumed input pins remain unchanged. Only this twelve-file research package is added.\n\n## Validation\n\nPython 3.10+, standard library; tested CPython 3.12.14, macOS arm64:\n\n~~~sh\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/r439-neutral-helper-chain-seed17/test_package.py\n~~~\n\nExpected: `PASS_R439_CHAIN_PACKAGE full_censuses=2 trials=32 controls=11 relocation=1 no_new_kappa`.\n\nBoth full censuses, all 32 full forward/reverse dirty-column trials, literal exporter/owner/frame and strict precision invoices pass. Thirteen primary semantic controls and eleven actual file-corruption controls reject, including wrong noncommuting order, omitted undo, undercharging, cap equality, duplicate keys and omission of a consumed source pin. Minimal offline relocation into a path with spaces and equivalent gzip repackaging pass; default replay preserves evidence and fails on missing evidence. Parent positive replay, selected-record guard, nine finite-bit-contract and five selected-result tests pass. Remote and staged Git trees match byte-for-byte. [Validation and unrun obligations](https://github.com/ToikY/integer-mult-bounds/blob/8d17ec366d4e4e50d8f28fdb3f23cf9213417b7a/research/r439-neutral-helper-chain-seed17/VALIDATION.md).\n\nNo Linux, Lean, independent human review, native multistage replay, full selected cold replay or hosted CI success is claimed. All-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source realization, physical hosting, precision/tape and analytic obligations remain. Selected frontier and upstream/ are unchanged.\n\n## Credit\n\nCredit Sagar Thakrar's PR1062 composition and PR1400/1206, Sricharan Vagvala's PR967, Gareth Davidson's PR915/926, Aaron Wang's PR1015, Ross Richardson's PR923/965, woklerx's PR1047 and semantic-D work, Hanson Sun's PR1449, and the DreamingOfClouds/eumemic/Dylan Crow lineage. [Sources and full credit](https://github.com/ToikY/integer-mult-bounds/blob/8d17ec366d4e4e50d8f28fdb3f23cf9213417b7a/research/r439-neutral-helper-chain-seed17/README.md). Prepared for **@ToikY with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance**, including separate bounded support-set and proof-review workers. AI implementations are not independent human review. Apache-2.0; predecessor notices remain untouched.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nCan a neutral chain remove a paid helper width rather than only scalar work? First derive both dirty-input and clean-response first-contact footprints across the actual chronology. The zero middle column alone cannot remove helper 570: preparation, undo and continuation still read it. A legal lifecycle and complete recursive invoice are blockers. This extension is not pursued here.\n",
